## Exceptions

```forth
100 throw          \ nonzero n always throws
3 0 ' / catch .    \ catch returns exception code (0 = ok)
```

Restore state on all exits — including exceptions:

```forth
: with-base ( xt -- )
  base @ >r
  try  execute 0  restore  r> base !  endtry  throw ;
```

Gforth `try … restore … endtry` is safe against async interrupts between `catch` and cleanup.

