## Development commands

```forth
see foo          \ decompile
.s               \ print stack
warnings         \ toggle warnings
```

## Structs (Gforth)

```forth
begin-structure point
  field: point.x
  field: point.y
end-structure
```

Match project field syntax; do not invent structures if the project uses plain offsets.

## What not to do

- No C `printf` or `"string\0"` unless binding C.
- Do not use `create` names as compile-time constants without `constant` / `literal` / `[']`.
- Use `char+` / `chars`, not hard-coded byte sizes.
